  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Provide examples of functions that have the following properties:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q14a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "strictly increasing and convex",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(x)=2^x$.",
          "worked": "One example is $f(x)=2^x$ on $\\mathbb{R}$. As $x$ increases, $2^x$ strictly increases, and its graph bends upwards, so it is convex.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q14b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "strictly increasing and concave",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(x)=-2^{-x}$.",
          "worked": "One example is $f(x)=-2^{-x}$ on $\\mathbb{R}$. As $x$ increases, $2^{-x}$ strictly decreases, so $-2^{-x}$ strictly increases. Reflecting the convex graph of $2^{-x}$ in the $x$-axis gives a concave graph.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q14c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "strictly decreasing and convex",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(x)=2^{-x}$.",
          "worked": "One example is $f(x)=2^{-x}$ on $\\mathbb{R}$. As $x$ increases, $2^{-x}$ strictly decreases. Its graph bends upwards, so it is convex.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q14d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "strictly decreasing and concave",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(x)=-2^x$.",
          "worked": "One example is $f(x)=-2^x$ on $\\mathbb{R}$. As $x$ increases, $2^x$ strictly increases, so $-2^x$ strictly decreases. Reflecting the convex graph of $2^x$ in the $x$-axis gives a concave graph.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
